  "title": "Portuguese Empire",
  "summary": "Portugal's colonial empire, the first established by a European power, began to take shape with the 1415 conquest of Ceuta. It eventually stretched from the Americas to Japan, often as a string of coastal bases. In 1498 Vasco da Gama opened a direct sea route to Asia. Its trade carried gold, spices and silk, and also enslaved people from Africa. It gave up Macao, its last colony, in 1999.",
